body:
This panics on a bare annotation when ty looks up `book.id`.

```python
from django.db import models

class Book(models.Model):
    class Meta:
        abstract: bool

def key(book: Book) -> int:
    return book.id
```

Django gives `Book` an integer `id`. Here the member's provenance points to the annotation, and `binding_type` panics because the annotation has no binding. I get a panic even if I add `abstract = True` on the next line. Could we read the bindings that reach the end of the `Meta` body so we pick up the actual value in both cases?

