I think I'm slightly confused by the high-level structure of the rule. I saw in crates/ruff_linter/src/checkers/ast/analyze/module.rs that the rule is being run on modules, but it seems that we're recursing into class scopes as well. I wonder if we should consider instead running the rule as part of [`deferred_scopes`](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/a83276d06966a36e895f26e86613064ea0c10147/crates/ruff_linter/src/checkers/ast/analyze/deferred_scopes.rs#L12) and checking for `ScopeKind::Class` and `ScopeKind::Module`.

Should we also consider recursing into functions? And does `organize_suite` handle further recursion like:

```py
class Foo:
	class Bar:
		def a(): ...

		def b(): return a()
```

Same with these, these functions are well-known and documented on the trait itself.


